# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2025-2026 Evgenij Cjura and project contributors
# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
#
# psram_bss.lf -- move the big fixed-size lookup tables out of internal DRAM.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
# ---------------
# Phase 1 added the esp-zigbee stack, and on esp32s31 that broke Ethernet:
#
#   E (1668) esp.emac.dma: emac_esp_new_dma(509): no mem for descriptors
#   E (1689) eth: board_eth_new failed: ESP_FAIL -- continuing with link down
#   E (2870) ws_server: httpd_start failed
#   E (2873) event_bus: queue alloc failed for type 11
#
# Not a Zigbee bug -- an internal-DRAM budget failure that Zigbee merely pushed
# over the line. The static picture before this file:
#
#   DIRAM  396360 / 503744 used (78.7%)  -> heap_init offered just 120 KiB
#   libzhc_adapter.a alone: 230 KB (106 KB .bss + 123 KB .data)
#
# EMAC DMA descriptors MUST come from internal DMA-capable memory, and they are
# allocated after the Zigbee stack has taken its share. Whoever asks last loses.
# Raising the allocation order would just move the failure onto Zigbee.
#
# WHAT MOVES
# ----------
# zhc_adapter's DRAM is dominated by a handful of fixed-size tables sized by
# max_devices/registry, not by anything per-frame:
#
#   56.5 KB  g_pool     (zhc_adapter_fallback.cpp)
#   32.7 KB  g_merged   (zhc_adapter.cpp)
#   10.4 KB  g_store    (zhc_adapter.cpp)
#    4.8 KB  g_slots    (zhc_adapter.cpp)
#
# These are decode-time lookup structures: no DMA, no ISR access, no use before
# app_main. That makes them exactly what extern_ram is for. PSRAM here runs at
# 250 MHz and there are 16 MB of it against ~120 KiB of contended internal DRAM,
# so the trade is heavily in our favour.
#
# WHAT MUST NOT MOVE -- THE RULE THIS FILE EXISTS TO RECORD
# ---------------------------------------------------------
# A buffer in PSRAM is reached THROUGH THE CACHE. Flash reads run with the
# cache disabled, so any buffer that a flash/NVS read writes into must stay in
# internal RAM. Break that and you get, at the first read of a key that
# actually exists:
#
#   Guru Meditation Error: Core 1 panic'ed (Cache error). Cache access error
#   MEPC 0x2f80d33c   (RA -> spi_flash_hal_read -> esp_flash_read)
#
# device_shadow was mapped here at first and did exactly this.
# device_shadow.cpp:269 reads straight into a static blob:
#
#   nvs_get_blob(s_nvs, key, s_attr_blob, &len);
#
# ...and s_attr_blob / s_sweep_blob / s_staged are precisely the .bss this
# fragment would have relocated. It survived one boot only because NVS was
# still empty; the crash arrived on the next boot, once a key had been written.
# An 18-deep reset loop for the sake of ~8 KB.
#
# So before adding an archive here, confirm it does no NVS reads, no flash
# reads and no DMA into static buffers. zhc_adapter qualifies: it contains no
# nvs_*, esp_flash_*, or esp_partition_* calls at all -- its tables are pure
# in-memory lookup state. That property is why only it is listed below.
#
# WHY A LINKER FRAGMENT AND NOT EXT_RAM_BSS_ATTR
# ----------------------------------------------
# EXT_RAM_BSS_ATTR would mean editing zhc_adapter, which lives in the sibling
# zhac-components repo. Those repos are read-only inputs to this SKU. A mapping
# fragment achieves the same placement from OUR side, so the shared component
# stays byte-identical for the flagship P4/S3 cores that do not need this.
#
# NOT FIXED HERE: libzhc_adapter.a also carries ~123 KB of .data spread across
# thousands of ~112-byte per-device symbols. Those look like definition structs
# that are not declared const, so they land in .data instead of .rodata (flash).
# Making them const would recover more internal DRAM than this whole file, but
# it is a change to the shared component -- raised as a ticket rather than
# patched here. `extram_bss` cannot help: .data needs its flash-image copy
# applied before PSRAM is mapped.
#
# APPLIES TO BOTH TARGETS. P4 has far more headroom, but the tables are just as
# idle there, and keeping one placement policy avoids a target-specific
# divergence nobody would remember to re-test.

[mapping:zhc_adapter_psram]
archive: libzhc_adapter.a
entries:
    * (extram_bss)
